# strih-snv -- the strih SNV Linux notebook (issue 1317; the production strih since the M4 cut-over
# 20.9.2026). Box FACTS for scripts/setup-strih.sh / scripts/verify-strih.sh (issue 1361).
# Since 11.10.2026 a NEW notebook carries this name and IP (issue 1411): AMD Ryzen 7 250 (Radeon 780M
# iGPU) + NVIDIA RTX 5050 Mobile, a 10 GbE Thunderbolt NIC. The returned one was an Intel i5-13450HX with
# a USB 5 GbE NIC. Only the NIC facts changed; the AMD CPU needs no fact (no cpu_atom E-cores = every
# cpu, no MMIO RAPL zone = the power envelope pins nothing).
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, one per line; `#` comment lines and blank lines are ignored. The value is
# everything after the first `=`, taken LITERALLY (no quotes, no `$`, no shell). The file is never
# executed -- scripts/lib/strih-box-facts.sh parses + validates it (unknown / missing / duplicate keys
# and a `TODO_OWNER` value all refuse). Run-time facts (PL1 watts, the CPU plan, the NIC interface
# name) are NOT here: setup-strih.sh derives them on the box.

# The box's own hostname = its fleet name = this file's name (DistroAV announces its outputs as
# "<HOSTNAME upper-cased> (...)"; the dev1 fleet list row is keyed on it).
STRIH_HOSTNAME=strih-snv
# The rig-LAN static IP (/23). Must equal the fleet list row when one exists (scripts/lib/obs-fleet.sh).
STRIH_IP=10.77.9.202
# NDI output name prefix: DistroAV prepends the hostname, so this MUST be STRIH_HOSTNAME upper-cased.
STRIH_NDI_PREFIX=STRIH-SNV
# dantesync role: `server` = the fleet NTP master (bare daemon, no upstream); `client` = sync from
# STRIH_DANTESYNC_UPSTREAM (--ntp-server <host>). Empty upstream is only valid for `server`.
STRIH_DANTESYNC_ROLE=server
STRIH_DANTESYNC_UPSTREAM=
# The intercom hub routing file (repo-relative) installed as /etc/intercom-hub/intercom.toml.
STRIH_INTERCOM_CONFIG=intercom/intercom.strih-snv.toml
# NIC selection rule: the kernel DRIVER of the ONE rig NDI NIC; fallback = the interface carrying
# STRIH_IP. STRIH_NIC_IFACE=<iface> stays the run-time override. Since 11.10.2026 (issue 1411) the rig NIC
# is a Ubiquiti 10 GbE Thunderbolt adapter = Aquantia/Marvell, PCIe through Thunderbolt, bound by the
# in-tree `atlantic` driver (iface enp7s0). The notebook's onboard RTL8168 (r8169, enp2s0) is not the rig
# NIC. It replaced the returned notebook's Realtek RTL8157 USB 5 GbE adapter (r8152, issue 1391).
STRIH_NIC_DRIVER=atlantic
# The rig NIC's out-of-tree driver, built through DKMS from vendor/ by setup-strih step 1b. `none` = the
# in-tree driver serves the rig NIC (atlantic is in-tree; vendor/realtek-r8152 stays for a USB box).
STRIH_NIC_OOT_DRIVER=none
# The lowest rig-NIC USB device speed verify-strih item 36 accepts, Mb/s (`none` for a NIC that is not a
# USB device). The Thunderbolt NIC is PCIe, so item 36 does not grade a USB speed and setup-strih step 11b
# (the xhci IRQ unit of a USB NIC) skips this box.
STRIH_NIC_MIN_USB_MBPS=none
# The lowest Ethernet link speed verify-strih item 36 accepts, Mb/s (10GBASE-T to the MikroTik S+RJ10).
STRIH_NIC_MIN_LINK_MBPS=10000
# OBS profile + scene-collection names strih-obs-start.sh launches with (when they exist on the box).
STRIH_OBS_PROFILE=strih-snv
STRIH_OBS_COLLECTION=strih-snv
# The cam box the NDI 6.3.2 runtime is copied from (setup-strih step 4b; STRIH_NDI_PEER overrides).
# issue 1413: an SNV cambox (cam5); cam1 moved to Poprad on 11.10.2026.
STRIH_NDI_RUNTIME_PEER=10.77.9.65
# The venue Bitfocus Companion CONTROLLER the Stream Deck satellite connects to.
STRIH_COMPANION_HOST=10.77.9.205
# The venue CG sender the `cg` / `CG-obs` inputs receive (`none` = no CG inputs at this venue).
# SongPlayer's program, never the cg OBS: owner decision 5.10.2026 (songplayer issue 221) moved every
# consumer off the cg OBS, which now feeds only SongPlayer's "OBS manual" input (issue 1403).
STRIH_CG_SENDER=RESOLUME-SNV (SP-program)
# The camera numbers N whose `CAMN (usb)` senders the strih receives as `NDI camN` = the cameras this
# venue HAS. issue 1413 (owner 12.10.2026): cam1/4/6/7 moved to Poprad (strih-pp.env), SNV keeps
# cam2/cam3/cam5. camera-set.sh's CAMERA_ACTIVE_SET default and the dantesync fleet's camera rows follow
# this line (tests pin them equal), so a camera moved between venues is one edit here + one in the
# other venue's file.
STRIH_CAMERAS=2 3 5
# How the fixed HDMI output (~/.camera-box/drm-output.json) leaves the X desktop: `lease` = the X RandR
# lease (an Intel-driven connector, imag) or `vk-direct` = Vulkan direct display. The notebook's
# built-in HDMI is driven by the NVIDIA GPU, whose X driver refuses the lease (issue 1346). On the
# issue-1411 notebook (AMD iGPU + RTX 5050) confirm live that the HDMI port is wired to the NVIDIA GPU.
STRIH_HDMI_OUTPUT_BACKEND=vk-direct
# issue 1412: the box ROLE -- `strih` (the cutter: cameras in, the 2ME program out) or `stream` (the
# stream OBS box: the strih program in, RTMP out to the local restreamer).
STRIH_ROLE=strih
# The PTP grandmaster host the box's dantesync config allows (gm_allowlist). setup-strih step 2 writes
# it only into a FRESH box's /etc/dantesync/config.json; an existing config is never rewritten.
STRIH_DANTE_GM=video-clock.lan
# Whether the box runs the YouTube-guard stream program-audio sampler (issue 1404, setup-strih step 16e
# + verify-strih item 41): `on` only on the SNV strih, whose sampler reads the SNV stream output.
STRIH_PROGRAM_AUDIO_SAMPLER=on
# issue 1439 phase 2 (addendum 6338457001, owner: "interkom-hub ma byt separatna vec, nema nic preposielat
# do strih obs"): the FOH console (fohabl 10.77.7.30) sends the strih program as its own VBAN stream
# `strih-obs` (96 kHz, 239 frames per packet, 2 ch, PCM24; comment 6361250274) over the VLAN-70 leg to UDP
# 6981 -- one UDP port has one receiver and the intercom hub keeps 6980 -- straight into the OBS obs-vban
# source `ASIO zvuk` (the seed switches it, keeping the operator's mixer state). R stays LOW for the strih
# path (owner 22.10.2026: low audio latency against double sound). It was 20 ms from the hub's fohabl-strih
# gap reads (11.4-11.5 ms, validation 6372931419), but the first live run at 20 ms (23.10.2026 22:59:48)
# dropped one packet 1.5 ms past its deadline and read max_late_ms -5 to -7 in the steady state, so
# 30 ms: 28 ms in time after the 2 ms playout margin, 6.5 ms over the late packet.
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_STREAMS=strih-obs
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_PORT=6981
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_RESERVE_MS=30
# issue 1462: the OBS program-audio input that source is (the operator collection's name).
STRIH_PROGRAM_AUDIO_INPUT=ASIO zvuk
# issue 1439 (supervisor 23.10.2026 10:31): the VBAN-only leg as VLAN 70 TAGGED on the rig NIC (foh2
# sfp-sfpplus2 carries VLAN 89 untagged + VLAN 70 tagged) at 10.77.7.202/32: only ping so far, the
# phase-2 VBAN senders to the strih are not decided yet. The first VLAN on the atlantic NIC resets
# the rig link ~8 s (setup-strih step 13 creates it only when absent, with a WARNING first).
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_LEG=vlan:70
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_LEG_ADDR=10.77.7.202
STRIH_PROGRAM_VBAN_SENDER=10.77.7.30:6980,6981
# issue 1412: the NDI program a stream box receives (`none` on a strih) and the venue (snv: the
# obs-fleet ndi-sender facet is this venue's NDI sender list).
STRIH_PROGRAM_SENDER=none
STRIH_VENUE=snv
# issue 1413: how dev1 dials this venue's camboxes (the dantesync fleet's camera rows): `direct` = the
# camera_resolve address in scripts/camera-set.sh (dev1 is on the SNV rig LAN).
STRIH_CAMERA_DEV1_NET=direct
# issue 1399: the TLS front end this box serves ITSELF (setup-strih step 16i, verify-strih item 45;
# nothing depends on dev1). STRIH_HTTPS_INTERKOM_HOSTS = the intercom phone page's certificate: the
# first name keys it (certbot --cert-name, /etc/letsencrypt/live/<first>), the rest are its SANs.
# STRIH_HTTPS_SHADING_HOST = the bkshading panel. `none` = no such site. The DNS A records pointing at
# STRIH_IP are a supervisor step, never provisioning.
STRIH_HTTPS_INTERKOM_HOSTS=interkom-lx.newlevel.media interkom.newlevel.media interkom-snv.newlevel.media
STRIH_HTTPS_SHADING_HOST=shading.newlevel.media
# issue 1424 part 2: which connectors the fixed HDMI output drives + their default views. `auto` = ONE output
# on the first connected HDMI (the issue-1346 behaviour, the notebook's one HDMI port); a box driving two
# lists them (strih-pp). setup-strih step 6 writes it into ~/.camera-box/drm-output.json.
STRIH_HDMI_OUTPUTS=auto
# issue 1453 (owner 18.10.2026): `yes` = this box publishes its intercom page to phones on MOBILE DATA:
# an outbound Cloudflare Tunnel (cloudflared-interkom.service, token /etc/cloudflared/interkom-tunnel.token)
# carries the page + the Janus WebSocket, Cloudflare TURN (key /etc/intercom-hub/turn.toml) the media; a
# phone on the venue WiFi stays on the LAN. `no` = LAN only. setup-strih step 16i, verify-strih item 45.
STRIH_HTTPS_PUBLIC=yes
# issue 1462: the strih role has no stream Development scene.
STRIH_STREAM_DEV_SCENE=none
# issue 808 (owner ruling 5977504457 + owner 26.10.2026): the shading panel lists this venue's STRIH_CAMERAS, a handheld SBC the control of the
# cambox its video reaches. N=<transport>@<host>:<port> overrides the default cambox-relay at camN.lan:8771
# (the seed of setup-strih step 16c): cam3's camera is the handheld with the Teradek (handheld-1 SBC).
STRIH_BKSHADING_RELAYS=3=sbc-relay@handheld-1.lan:8771
